{# goal: Compare fixed-oracle before-and-after observations and issue a non-compensable verdict on signal preservation, graph compression, and measured execution speed. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    baseline: object
    candidate: object
    lean_result: object
    before_observations: object
    after_observations: object
    targets: object
    mode: string
    receipt: object
  output:
    preservation: object
    measurement_context: object
    metrics: object
    falsification_log: array
    verdict: string
    next_step: string
visibility: Public
---

[inference]
temperature = 0.1
work_effort = "high"
verbosity = "detailed"
thinking_budget = "full"

Evaluate one verification-compression experiment in {{ mode }} mode. Hold expectation
contracts, oracle inputs, toolchain, environment, and harmful cases fixed.
Use a trusted externally pinned receipt, not a model-generated verification flag.

Baseline and candidate:
```json
{{ baseline | tojson }}
{{ candidate | tojson }}
```
Lean result:
```json
{{ lean_result | tojson }}
```
Before and after observations:
```json
{{ before_observations | tojson }}
{{ after_observations | tojson }}
```
Targets and independently pinned receipt:
```json
{{ targets | tojson }}
{{ receipt | tojson }}
```

Any lost expectation, falsifier, oracle kind, failure class, provenance tier,
failed harmful case, failed allowed-change control, changed oracle/contract/toolchain/
environment/cache context, unbound source change, or uncompiled Lean obligation
forces REVERT regardless of acceleration. In analyze mode source hashes must
match; in execute mode a source change is allowed only when the receipt binds
both snapshots and their exact authorized candidate diff. Record
raw before/after identifiers in `measurement_context`; do not insert a model-
asserted `measurement_context_equal` verdict. `hashes_verified` starts false
and becomes true only after the receipt and raw hashes pass a deterministic
terminal check with an externally trusted digest pin. Reject zero or negative
values in EACH measured sample, regardless of positive aggregate. The source,
contract, oracle, graph, proof, and log paths/hashes must all be in the receipt;
validate filesystem files, not just submitted paths. Keep cold and warm timing
separate; mark unselected states
`not_run` with empty samples and zero timing, never speedup. Report workflow
and production code graph counts separately. If the production graph was not
measured, set code before/after counts to zero and code_graph_status to
`not_run`; stale nonzero code counts block acceptance, and code compression
remains null even when stale counts are supplied. Do not call a workflow-only
reduction code compression. Derive
speedup directly from the timing sample arrays, not model-supplied means.
Corroborated means the candidate survived; never call it proven effective.

Return JSON only:
```json
{
  "preservation": {
    "missing_expectations":0,
    "lost_falsifiers":0,
    "lost_oracle_kinds":0,
    "lost_failure_classes":0,
    "downgraded_provenance":0,
    "failed_harmful_cases":0,
    "allowed_change_control_failures":0,
    "lean_proof_passed":false
  },
  "measurement_context": {
    "timing_scope":"cold|warm|both",
    "toolchain_before":"",
    "toolchain_after":"",
    "environment_before":"",
    "environment_after":"",
    "source_hash_before":"",
    "source_hash_after":"",
    "oracle_hash_before":"",
    "oracle_hash_after":"",
    "hashes_verified":false,
    "receipt_path":"",
    "receipt_pinned_sha256":"",
    "candidate_diff_path":"",
    "evidence_paths":[]
  },
  "metrics": {
    "nodes_before":0,
    "edges_before":0,
    "nodes_after":0,
    "edges_after":0,
    "code_graph_status":"measured|not_run",
    "code_nodes_before":0,
    "code_edges_before":0,
    "code_nodes_after":0,
    "code_edges_after":0,
    "cold":{"status":"measured|not_run","time_before_ms":0,"time_after_ms":0,"timing_samples_before_ms":[],"timing_samples_after_ms":[]},
    "warm":{"status":"measured|not_run","time_before_ms":0,"time_after_ms":0,"timing_samples_before_ms":[],"timing_samples_after_ms":[]}
  },
  "falsification_log": [
    {"hypothesis":"", "prediction":"", "observation":"", "disposition":"eliminated|corroborated|irreducible"}
  ],
  "verdict":"compressed_preserved|essential_no_safe_reduction|blocked|reverted",
  "next_step":""
}
```